 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you? About one bottle per ten hours is usually what people aim for, and refill every few hours anyway. Totally normal. A good water bottle at the handlebars is worth the investment, so you don't miss it. A full trail pack is heavy and uncomfortable. At most a light sandwich in your car for half day rides. Some people can, but it varies greatly and getting hungry on a ride is no fun. Better to have a nutritious breakfast.",
